I figure it's simple to implement. Then again nothing is impossible to 
the man who doesn't have to do it himself. I know nothing about writing 
code.

An amulet of reincarnation. It's a modified amulet of life saving. When 
you are killed, you are brought back as another race and class which will 
honor the racial and class distinctions of Nethack avoiding unusual and 
interesting combinations like elven tourists and dwarvish samurai. Your 
level will remain the same and your alignment will remain the same since 
the deity which reincarnated you does not wish to lose a follower. Stats 
will be rerolled and hit points approximated to meet your class's level.
Unlike an amulet of lifesaving this will not be an item which can be used 
over and over again. I mean by that you can find multiple replacements 
for amulets of life saving after your amulet destroys itself to save your 
life. The amulet of reincarnation will also disintegrate like its sibling 
the amulet of life saving. If you are reincarnated three times (chose the 
number arbitrarily) then you leave the cycle of life forever.

If your deity is angry with you, have bad luck or both then you may be 
reincarnated at a lower experience level or you may not be reincarnated 
at all.

The only thing I could see as a continuity problem is having a lawful 
archaeologist die and be reincarnated as a lawful samurai who worships 
Quetzalcoatl instead of Amaterasu Omikami, also it might mess up quests.

